    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Certificates and Chain of Trust with Bouncy Castle',
         body=None,
         narration='Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains certificates and the chain of trust, with Bouncy Castle and OpenSSL, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] A certificate is a public key with a name, signed by an authority. [[slnc 300]] A chain of trust is a path of such signatures, from a certificate you want to trust, to a root you already trust. [[slnc 600]] Think of a passport office. [[slnc 300]] The government authorises regional offices, and can limit what each may issue. [[slnc 300]] The traveller brings only a form, never the pen they sign with. [[slnc 300]] And lost passports are published on a list. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is an online store. [[slnc 500]] By the end, you will hear how to build a chain with a library. [[slnc 300]] How an authority is limited. [[slnc 300]] How certificates are withdrawn. [[slnc 300]] And what a stolen authority key does.'),
